  "type": "numerical",
  "level": 1,
  "question": {
    "text": "The maximum and minimum amplitude of an amplitude modulated wave is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>8</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></math> respectively. The modulation index for this amplitude modulated wave is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></math>. The value of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math> is _______. (Round off your answer to the nearest integer)",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [],
  "correctValue": "33",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Modulation index <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>-</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>A</mi><mi>min</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>-</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>16</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>8</mn><mn>24</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mn>3</mn></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>33</mn></math></p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi><mo>&#215;</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>33</mn></math></p>So, $x=33$",
    "image": null
  },
